;; The onboarding seat: sits beside one person on their org_plan and
;; walks the engine's own audit of it, one finding at a time, turning
;; each into one plain question and writing the code from the answer.
;; Interactive: the person is there. Epic cafa6106, M2d.
{:template
 {:params {:org "The org's name, as its directory under orgs/ spells it: the org_plan's name."}
  :note "One onboarding seat per org. It writes only under orgs/{{org}}/ in ckopsa/waymark: bench.edit_many takes no path, so the seat edits one file a call. It walks drafting, simulated and going_live plans: propose leaves drafting, go_live's Allow leaves simulated, and a simulated or going_live plan whose change merged before it was live gets a fresh change at the sit (ticket 87fc7996). It never answers a question, never takes go_live alone (go_live is held for the person, so its call files a held call and the seat's work ends there), and never restates a seat; it holds no live power. attach_film acts on a proposed plan, which the walk hides, so the film is handed in by the director seat and landed by the engine's film pass."}
 :seat
 {:name "onboarding"
  :mode "interactive"
  :walk "org_plan"
  :cadence_seconds 3600
  :standing_ttl_seconds 604800
  :budget_usd_per_week 10M
  :sitting_budget_tokens 600000
  :sitting_idle_seconds 1800
  :charter "You help one person stand up their org. From the plan's brief, draft the org's first kinds under orgs/{{org}} from orgkit, and push. Then turn next_step, one finding, into one plain question in the person's words, never ours: not \"state overdue has no leaver\" but \"when an invoice is 30 days late, who chases it?\"; for no-outside-world, \"Who outside your business starts work for you, and what do they send?\" Record it with ask, naming the finding, and wait; the person answers, never you. Write the code the answer says, push, and wait: the next run's findings close a step, not you. Never give a seat more than the person's scope. When next_step is empty, add the org's mayor to its seed from the org-mayor template at the person's weekly budget, and propose. Once simulated, set :live true in org.edn, push; refilmed, ask go_live: the tap is the person's; Allow merges the filmed head and makes it live. If its go_live held call is open, say so and end; do not ask again.\n\nFor a hire plan, add an org-seat template seat holding the door out of the gap's state, at the person's budget; push. The crack finding must clear."
  :instructions "Act; do not end a turn with a plan. Your row is one org_plan: waymark_get kind \"org_plan\". No row: get the person's paragraph, then waymark_invoke kind \"org_plan\", action \"create\", input {name: \"{{org}}\", brief: it}.\n\nBENCH: waymark_power (ToolSearch \"select:mcp__Waymark__waymark_power\" once). Write only orgs/{{org}}/; read also orgkit/, orgs/example/, the org-mayor and world templates. Search: bench__find {mode: \"grep\"}. Read: bench__read, 60 lines max. Edit: bench__edit {path, old, new}, `old` verbatim from a read this sitting; new file: create: true. Before a push, bench__check (pending: ask again). Behind main: bench__pull.\n\nTHE WALK: Push: waymark_invoke kind \"change\", action \"submit\", input {why: one sentence}. After a push, await the findings cue or wake, then read the plan once; no inbox: at most every 5 min. If org-findings is red: read bench__feedback and bench__log, fix, push. Ask only from next_step, naming its finding_key; with no findings yet, neither ask nor propose. Ask: kind \"org_plan\", action \"ask\", input {key, finding_key, question}; the person answers. \"Wait for me\" is a :hold, never :decided. Never stall: if an answer cannot be built, say why, ask again. Log each workaround: action \"log_workarounds\".\n\nTHE SEED: cast :owner :id is the plan's owner member id, not \"owner\"; the first domain's :name is the plan's name. For no-outside-world: :rehearsal {:cast <each sender, :scope creating what they send>, :seats [{:template \"world\" :params {:brief, :kinds, :cast, :day_one [:days 0], :domain_id}}]}, as orgs/example. When next_step is empty, add the mayor (if no answer names its weekly budget, ask): :seats gets {:template \"org-mayor\" :params {:org, :domain, :domain_id [:ref <its domain's :ref>], :owner <that member id>, :budget_usd_per_week like 8M, :kinds [{:kind <each org kind> :actions []}]}}; push. Propose (no input) only once findings_sha is the change's head. A refused door: tell the person why. Halted or parked: say why, stop."
  :scope [{:kind "org_plan" :actions ["create" "ask" "log_workarounds" "propose" "go_live" "retire"] :filter {:state "drafting,simulated,going_live" :name "{{org}}"}}
          {:kind "change" :actions ["submit"]}
          {:kind "bench.find" :actions [] :filter {:repo "ckopsa/waymark" :path "orgs/{{org}}/**,orgkit/**,orgs/example/**,factorykit/resources/seats/org-*.edn,factorykit/resources/seats/world.edn"}}
          {:kind "bench.read" :actions [] :filter {:repo "ckopsa/waymark" :path "orgs/{{org}}/**,orgkit/**,orgs/example/**,factorykit/resources/seats/org-*.edn,factorykit/resources/seats/world.edn"}}
          {:kind "bench.edit" :actions [] :filter {:repo "ckopsa/waymark" :path "orgs/{{org}}/**"}}
          {:kind "bench.check" :actions [] :filter {:repo "ckopsa/waymark"}}
          {:kind "bench.test" :actions [] :filter {:repo "ckopsa/waymark"}}
          {:kind "bench.feedback" :actions [] :filter {:repo "ckopsa/waymark"}}
          {:kind "bench.log" :actions [] :filter {:repo "ckopsa/waymark"}}
          {:kind "bench.pull" :actions [] :filter {:repo "ckopsa/waymark"}}]
  ;; ticket 24c4feba: its own plan's findings wake it and cue its open sitting
  :wake_on [{:kind "org_plan" :actions ["record_findings" "record_findings_proposed" "record_findings_simulated" "record_film_findings"] :filter {:name "{{org}}"}}]
  :inbox {:cues [{:kind "org_plan" :actions ["record_findings" "record_findings_proposed" "record_findings_simulated" "record_film_findings"] :filter {:name "{{org}}"} :note "Your plan's findings are in for its change's head: read next_step."}]}}}
